  exp: "Cervical screening aims to identify high-risk HPV infection or precancerous cervical lesions before invasive cancer develops, enabling appropriate triage and treatment. Screening eligibility, test choice, intervals, and follow-up should follow current national or local guidance. Symptoms such as postcoital bleeding require diagnostic evaluation even if screening is not due.",
  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Definitive diagnosis of invasive cancer):</strong> Screening tests are not definitive diagnostic tests for every individual; abnormal findings may require further evaluation.<br>• <strong>Option C (Replace diagnostic evaluation):</strong> Screening is intended for asymptomatic populations and does not replace assessment of concerning symptoms.<br>• <strong>Option D (No follow-up after a negative test):</strong> Appropriate repeat screening and follow-up remain necessary according to the recommended schedule and individual risk."
