  ans: 0,
  exp: "Vitamin A is essential for the visual cycle and maintenance of normal epithelial tissues. Deficiency can cause night blindness and xerophthalmia, progressing in severe cases to corneal damage and blindness. Prevention and treatment depend on age-appropriate vitamin A supplementation, dietary improvement, and management of associated illness according to guidance.",
  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option B (Vitamin B12):</strong> Deficiency primarily causes megaloblastic anemia and neurological manifestations rather than classic xerophthalmia.<br>• <strong>Option C (Vitamin D):</strong> Deficiency impairs bone mineralization and causes rickets in children.<br>• <strong>Option D (Vitamin K):</strong> Deficiency impairs coagulation factor activation and can cause bleeding."
