  exp: "Risk among smokers = 100/1,000 = 0.10. Risk among nonsmokers = 20/1,000 = 0.02. Relative risk = 0.10/0.02 = 5. Therefore, the correct answer is 5.",
  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (2):</strong> This is not the ratio of the two cumulative risks.<br>• <strong>Option B (5):</strong> This is the correct relative risk because 0.10 divided by 0.02 equals 5.<br>• <strong>Option D (20):</strong> This compares the number of smoker cases with nonsmoker cases without appropriately accounting for the group denominators."
