  ans: 0,
  exp: "The Mann–Whitney U test is a rank-based nonparametric test for comparing two independent groups. It can assess differences in distributions and, under appropriate assumptions about distributional shape, differences in location. It is often considered when a continuous or ordinal outcome is unsuitable for a conventional independent-samples t-test.",
  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option B (Paired t-test):</strong> This is designed for paired continuous observations and relies on assumptions about the distribution of paired differences.<br>• <strong>Option C (McNemar test):</strong> This is used for paired categorical data, particularly binary outcomes.<br>• <strong>Option D (Repeated-measures ANOVA):</strong> This compares repeated continuous measurements across conditions or time points in related participants."
